# beatmania IIDX Substream with DDR 2nd Club Version 2 (GE984 A01 BM), Konami 1999: the club kit's IIDX
# cabinet (Substream's board, twinklex2). First power-on from blank NVRAM: "GE984JA DEVICE CHECK"
# passes everything but the backup RAM, E150 BACKUP DATA ERROR, then "1P START = BACKUP CLEAR" (by
# ~3100). 1P Start clears it and the game goes on to attract (unlike Club Version 1's, this clear
# works). Hashes the main RAM every frame and snapshots every 60 frames, for lockstep with MAME
# (stock, at the pin). No DDR cabinet on the link (the PS1's SIO1 here).
game bmiidxc2

hash ram  0x80000000 0x80400000   # 4 MiB main RAM (KSEG0)

at 3600 press "1 Player Start" 8
from 0 every 60 snap
at 10000 quit
